OpenCode tool wire definitions

Upstream: https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode
Release: v2.0.29
Commit: 042d0832f5f3a73eaa039a58a7d565776f6d4290

The descriptions and parameter schemas originate in the MIT-licensed official
OpenCode client. Source definitions were checked directly against:
https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode/tree/042d0832f5f3a73eaa039a58a7d565776f6d4290/packages/core/src/tool/plugin
https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode/blob/042d0832f5f3a73eaa039a58a7d565776f6d4290/packages/core/src/codemode/tool.ts
https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode/blob/042d0832f5f3a73eaa039a58a7d565776f6d4290/packages/schema/src/question.ts

The JSON is a concrete CLI wire snapshot, including runtime-expanded shell and
subagent descriptions. Snapshot reference: jasonxu114514/opencode2api commit
25afadd30345faaa9c6f18c45c0c14b176862b89, internal/gateway/opencode_tools.json.
Local modification: the shell description drops the snapshot host's
"Commands run on Windows using powershell." sentence.
No GPL proxy implementation is included; ccLoad's request shaping is independent.

